{
  "contract": "explanation-effective-cases/1",
  "what": "The shared cases for design/explanation/spec.md \u00a73.2, the effective-explanation rule. The TypeScript selection function (mcp-server/src/invariants.ts selectExplanation, run by mcp-server/test-explanations.mjs) and the Python one in the materializer both run every case, so the Python gate needs no built server.",
  "how_to_read": "rows is the set of stored rows for one (subject_type, subject_id, slot), in no guaranteed order. eligible is whether the subject is explanation-eligible. workspace is whether a workspace is bound; when it is, resolvable lists the ref_sha values it can resolve, and when it is not the field is absent and nothing can be resolved. expect gives the state (recorded, declined, not-recorded), the id of the effective row or null, and whether the reading is checked. kind groups the cases: superseded, declined, withdrawn, unreachable, no-workspace, ineligible, empty. subject_eligibility is the rule that supplies eligible: a subsystem by its own status, the project by whether any subsystem is eligible, which is the condition its account is written under. Both languages run those cases too. workspace_binding is the rule that supplies workspace: a path is bound when git reports it inside a work tree, so a directory that is no repository, a path that does not exist and a repository whose metadata has gone all read as no workspace. Each kind names how a gate builds the path.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "superseded",
      "kind": "superseded",
      "description": "a later row at a later commit replaces an earlier one",
      "eligible": true,
      "workspace": true,
      "resolvable": [
        "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
        "bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "disposition": "recorded",
          "ref_sha": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "disposition": "recorded",
          "ref_sha": "bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb"
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "state": "recorded",
        "row_id": 2,
        "checked": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "same-commit-correction",
      "kind": "superseded",
      "description": "a correction written at the same commit as the row it replaces is effective; the greatest id decides, not the revision",
      "eligible": true,
      "workspace": true,
      "resolvable": [
        "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "disposition": "recorded",
          "ref_sha": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "disposition": "recorded",
          "ref_sha": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "state": "recorded",
        "row_id": 2,
        "checked": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "rows-out-of-order",
      "kind": "superseded",
      "description": "the rows arrive in no particular order; the greatest id still decides",
      "eligible": true,
      "workspace": true,
      "resolvable": [
        "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa",
        "bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": 3,
          "disposition": "recorded",
          "ref_sha": "bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb"
        },
        {
          "id": 1,
          "disposition": "recorded",
          "ref_sha": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "disposition": "declined",
          "ref_sha": "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa"
        }
      ],
      "expect": {
        "state": "recorded",
        "row_id": 3,
        "checked": true
      }
    },
